load @term/seed/structure/ring
  find ring

# The Weyl algebra: the algebra of polynomial differential operators, generated by multiplication by a coordinate and
# differentiation with respect to it, satisfying the canonical commutation relation (differentiating then multiplying
# exceeds multiplying then differentiating by one). It is the algebraic home of quantization. The form carries the
# underlying ring.
form weyl-algebra
  link ring, like ring
